    "L6_integrity_profiles": "confident but spiritually rotten; high-claim, low-support; precise but lifeless; conceptually fertile but under-tested; publication-ready but adversarially incomplete",
    "L6_top_supported_1": "David Lowe · POF 2828 · Theophysics Research Program\n\nThe Convergence Series · March 2026\n\n\"The days of our years are threescore years and ten; and if by reason of strength they be fourscore years, yet is their strength labour and sorrow; for it is soon cut off, and we fly away.\"\n\n— Psalm 90:10\n\n\"LORD, you have been our dwelling place throughout all generations.\"\n\n— Psalm 90:1\n\nχ = ∭(G·M·E·S·T·K·R·Q·F·C) dx dy dt\n\nPOF 2828 · Theophysics · David Lowe · 15 + 15 = 100",
    "L6_top_supported_2": "When you plot these lifespans against generation number and fit an exponential decay model, you get this:\n\n$$L(n) = L\\_0 \\cdot e^{-n/\\tau} + L\\_{\\text{floor}}$$\n\nL(n)\nLifespan at generation *n* — how long people lived\n\nL0\nPre-decay baseline — the starting point before the decay\n\ne-n/τ\nExponential decay — compounding entropy across generations\n\nτ\nDecay timescale — ~3–4 generations for lifespan to drop to ~37% of L0\n\nLfloor\nThe asymptotic floor — **the minimum lifespan that entropy cannot breach**\n\nLifespans drop off the cliff after the Flood following a precise exponential curve — not a random scattering, not a linear decline, but the specific shape you get when something is compounding generation by generation — and then they level off and stop dropping around a specific floor.",
    "L6_top_risky_1": "A gradual erosion produces a roughly straight downward line.",
    "L6_top_risky_2": "He always was closer than the model.",
